{"content":[{"c":["NAIOTH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Place where David was given refuge from Saul (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.19.18-20.1","r":"1Sam.19.18-20.1","rawR":"1Sam.19.18-20.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.19.18-20.1","value":"1Sam.19.18-20.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 19:18–20:1"},"). Here Samuel supervised a group of prophets. According to verses ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.19.19","r":"1Sam.19.19","rawR":"1Sam.19.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.19.19","value":"1Sam.19.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"19"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.19.23","r":"1Sam.19.23","rawR":"1Sam.19.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.19.23","value":"1Sam.19.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"23"}," of chapter ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.19.1-24","r":"1Sam.19.1-24","rawR":"1Sam.19.1-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.19.1-24","value":"1Sam.19.1-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"19"},", Naioth was located within Ramah, Samuel’s hometown."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The derivation of the term is enigmatic. The word occurs nowhere else in Scripture, and the Hebrew text seems intentionally obscure. The word perhaps stems from a Hebrew root meaning “pastoral abode” or “dwelling place.” In ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.15.25","r":"2Sam.15.25","rawR":"2Sam.15.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.15.25","value":"2Sam.15.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Samuel 15:25"}," another derivative of the Hebrew root refers to the Lord’s habitation, prompting some to suggest that Naioth is a proper noun referring to a sanctuary in Ramah (see ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.10.5","r":"1Sam.10.5","rawR":"1Sam.10.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.10.5","value":"1Sam.10.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 10:5"},", where prophets were also associated with a sanctuary). Others conclude that Naioth alludes to a school, cloister, or settlement of prophets, of which Samuel was head."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Naioth","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Sm 19:18–20:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.19.18-20.1","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.19.18-20.1","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.19.18-20.1"},{"anchorText":"19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.19.19","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.19.19","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.19.19"},{"anchorText":"23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.19.23","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.19.23","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.19.23"},{"anchorText":"19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.19.1-24","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.19.1-24","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.19.1-24"},{"anchorText":"2 Samuel 15:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.15.25","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.15.25","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.15.25"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 10:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.10.5","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.10.5","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.10.5"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6313ffdcfac14633a7ef79ce1b572a55b175b21285a53e20987a0a980b625872","sourceItemName":"Naioth","sourceItemOrder":39,"sourceMember":"Articles/N.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Naioth","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Naioth","title":"Naioth","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}